diff --git a/website/docs/developer-guide/plugins/agent-runtime-plugin.md b/website/docs/developer-guide/plugins/agent-runtime-plugin.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..e984c5a8cbf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/website/docs/developer-guide/plugins/agent-runtime-plugin.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+---
+title: Native agent runtime plugins
+---
+
+A model-provider plugin can opt into owning a complete turn with
+`ProviderProfile.agent_runtime`. The default empty string keeps the existing
+model-only provider behavior. A nonempty string names the plugin settings key;
+`create_agent_runtime(cwd, state, settings, environment)` returns an
+`agent.native_runtime.NativeAgentRuntime` instance.
+
+The host keeps its normal durable turn lease, profile scope, stream callbacks,
+Desktop transport and display transcript. It forwards only the current user input
+to the runtime. The runtime owns its prompt, native tools, history, compaction and
+process. Hermes does not construct a model client or execute projected tool calls
+on this route. Vendor code stays in a standalone plugin.
+
+Implement these synchronous methods:
+
+| Method | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `run_turn(message, *, model)` | Yield normalized display/control events, ending with one terminal `result`. One turn at a time. |
+| `respond(request_id, response)` | Resolve a permission or question requested by the runtime. |
+| `interrupt()` | Request native cancellation without waiting for a new turn or replaying the interrupted request. |
+| `close()` | Release owned resources. Retain native persisted history for explicit resume. |
+
+The input is either text or Hermes's multipart user content. Runtime plugins
+validate the formats they support before sending them. The supplied environment
+is profile-scoped and filtered through the normal subprocess environment policy;
+a SDK which merges the parent environment must not reintroduce removed secrets.
+
+Events have a `type` and the following fields:
+
+| Type | Fields |
+| --- | --- |
+| `session` | `state`: native `session_id`, exact `cwd`, and plugin-specific resume metadata. |
+| `text_delta`, `reasoning_delta` | `text`. |
+| `assistant` | `text`, optional `reasoning`, optional OpenAI-shaped `tool_calls` for display. |
+| `tool_start` | Native `id`, `name`, `input`. |
+| `tool_result` | Same `id`, `name`, `input`, string `content`, optional `is_error`. |
+| `status` | `text`. |
+| `request` | `id`, `kind` (`permission` or `question`), native `tool`, `input`; questions also include `questions` with Hermes `qid`, `question`, `choices`, `multi_select`. |
+| `result` | `text`, optional `error`, `interrupted`, native token `usage`, `api_calls`. |
+
+Permissions use Hermes's existing human approval gate. Questions use the agent's
+existing clarification callback. Missing clients and missing answers deny requests.
+The plugin receives `{allowed, message}` and, for questions, an `answer` object.
+Native provider permissions which already permit an operation need not emit a request.
+
+The host persists resume state in `session.model_config.native_agent_runtime`
+(version 1). It binds it to its Hermes owner, provider, runtime kind and workspace,
+and records the display tail UID. Copied native identities and rewound mirrors
+are refused; native history is never recreated from the display mirror. A native
+runtime cannot be selected in an existing model-only conversation. Model changes
+within the same runtime preserve its process and native identity.
+
+Hermes manual compression is refused, crash recovery never automatically resends
+native tasks, and model-only auxiliary requests require a separate provider.
+Runtime plugins currently require `plugins.isolation: in_process`; there is no
+cross-plugin-host session transport in this version.
+
+A runtime profile may also expose the native CLI's own slash commands by implementing
+`slash_commands(*, cwd, runtime)`, returning `{name, description, args_hint?, kind?}`
+rows (`kind` is `command` or `skill`; `runtime` is the chat's live runtime or `None`).
+Hermes lists them first in the slash menu of chats on that provider and sends
+`/name args` to the native agent as the turn's prompt; the runtime interprets it. A
+name Hermes already owns keeps its Hermes meaning, and the native command is offered
+as `/<slash_namespace>:<name>` (the profile attribute; default: the provider name).
+The listing runs per keystroke, so it must answer from a cache.
